{
  "id": "COMPOUND:43496 - PROTEIN:5943",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between the compound (2S,3R)-3-hydroxy-6-(2-hydroxyethyl)-2,5,7-trimethyl-2,3-dihydroinden-1-one and the protein tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP, as it is identified as a target of multiple compounds that ultimately act on this enzyme. SNU-387, a cell line, is targeted by Dendocarbin K and another compound, 5-[[(2S,3R,4R)-4-(1,3-benzodioxol-5-ylmethyl)-2-methoxyoxolan-3-yl]methyl]-1,3-benzodioxole, both of which have a target of the LC-PTP. Additionally, 5-Hydroxytryptophan monohydrate, dl- is also targeted by the compound, and this target is also LC-PTP. The evidence suggests that the compound may act through a mechanism that involves targeting SNU-387, which in turn may influence the activity of LC-PTP. The core mechanism appears to involve the inhibition of LC-PTP, as multiple compounds with a similar structure are shown to target this enzyme. The evidence is consistent with a direct interaction between the compound and the enzyme, but further validation is needed to confirm the exact mechanism and the extent of the compound's effect on LC-PTP.",
